  "body": "Stacked on #2904 (merge #2904 first)\n\nThe prerequisite merged as bac4a96c while this work was in progress.\nThe merge-base diff now contains only the changes for #2845.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Link contact-face fragments only when a four-use edge has one complete matching.\n- Keep existing two-use bodies together. Check all shared edges after the links.\n- Preserve the closure, winding and outward-volume checks.\n- Keep all incident facets until the feature graph checks the contact. Emit one facet pair for each valid solid.\n- Store two edge uses inline. Allocate extra storage only for edges with more uses.\n- Enable both known-fail pins for #2845. Add geometry pins for whole-face contact and line-only refusal.\n- Require a contour over two closed solids in one model to match the single-block reference cut.\n\n## Cause\n\nA contact face can have no plain boundary edge. Plain-edge links then leave that face apart from its solid.\nThe feature graph kept only three incident facets. It marked every edge with more than two uses as non-manifold.\n\nThe old stitching test called two complete outward cubes one self-touching body because they shared one model.\nThat fixture is the legal whole-face contact case in this issue. The updated test compares the complete cut and verification result.\n\n## Tests\n\nThese four pins failed on unchanged production code. They passed after the fix:\n\n- `solids_that_touch_face_to_face_are_two_outward_bodies`\n- `no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture`\n- `solids_sharing_a_whole_face_slice_as_one_outline`\n- `a_whole_contact_face_keeps_each_solids_features`\n\n`sample_ap214.step` had 216 tangent edge pairs that picked apart. The pin now finds none.\nThe face-to-face stack changed from one `NonManifold` verdict to two `Outward` bodies.\n\nThe pairing unit tests pass. They cover ambiguity, odd and unbalanced uses, zero edges, invalid apices and pinched bodies.\nThe full winding, feature, slicing and shared-face safety suites pass. The sample generates finish and pocket paths with no gouge.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- Restore the old upstream slicer caller: the slice pin fails. Restore the fix: it passes.\n- Restore the old upstream winding caller: the winding pin fails. Restore the fix: it passes.\n- Restore the old upstream feature builder: the feature pin fails. Restore the fix: it passes.\n- Restore the parent's old slicer: `touching_closed_solids_in_one_model_cut_as_their_union` fails. Restore the fix: it passes.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` selected the batch plan. It completed 972 steps.\n971 steps passed. The only failure was the old refusal assertion for the legal whole-face contact fixture.\nAfter that expected-change test was updated, the failed-step gate passed all six `stitch_cross` tests.\nProduction code did not change between these gate runs.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe full gate's clippy check also passed for all eight crates.\n\n## Final-head verification requested by review\n\nHead: `75afc26f19d06abd752517a449a46d38c362f5af`.\nThe head and source files did not change during these checks.\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` reached the motion and app heavy lanes.\nThe command completed 229 steps in 65.8 minutes and exited with status 1.\n228 steps passed or produced the expected result for a known-fail pin. One step had an unexpected failure.\n\n| Heavy lane | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Motion | 56 tests passed. Two known-fail pins failed as expected. |\n| App | 40 tests passed. Five known-fail pins failed as expected. One test failed unexpectedly. |\n\nAll six sample bands in `shared_face_bodies_finish` passed with no gouge.\n\nThe unexpected failure was `app pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`.\nIt stopped at `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:144:5` with the path tuple `(3158, 3130, 1141)`.\nThe diagnostic reported 3158 moves, 3130 planar moves and 1141 arcs.\nIts notes said that some fitted arcs could not be proved inside the cutter-centre area and stayed as chords.\nThe heavy gate is red. These results do not establish whether this PR caused the failure.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` selected the batch plan and passed all 972 steps in 91.5 minutes.\nAll nine prebuilds and the all-target clippy checks for eight crates passed.\nAll nine `stock_source_holes` tests passed, including `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number`.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe tracked files and goldens stayed unchanged.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. This PR changes no `.nc` or `.cl` file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe full release gate and manual GUI use were not exercised.\nNewer upstream-only commits were not merged into this branch.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThis branch started from the open PR #2904 at 853522f2e. That PR has now merged.\nThe shared functions are `shared_edge::solids_touch`, `slice_bodies::closed_solids` and `pick::winding::touching_solids`.\nThe two restored regression tests also overlap that prerequisite. No other open overlap was found.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Touching closed solids retain their contact faces and complete feature edges.\n\nFixes #2845\n",
